53
01:18:14.434 --> 01:18:16.434
This is what Jacob said.

54
01:18:16.434 --> 01:18:22.434
And Jacob was changed from deceiver to he who continues with God in the struggle of life.

55
01:18:22.434 --> 01:18:27.434
Jacob becomes Israel. And the people of Israel arise.

56
01:18:27.434 --> 01:18:35.434
Israel eventually moves to Egypt due to a famine.

57
01:18:35.434 --> 01:18:39.434
They end up in misery and slavery for 400 years.

58
01:18:39.434 --> 01:18:47.434
And through Moses, Israel is freed from Egypt in the chaos they are in.

59
01:18:47.434 --> 01:18:50.434
And they are ultimately brought to the promised land.

60
01:18:50.434 --> 01:18:57.434
That land where God said to Abraham in the beginning, I will bring you to a better place.

61
01:18:57.434 --> 01:19:04.434
So Abraham was not yet there in that promised land in the fullness of the promise.

62
01:19:04.434 --> 01:19:07.434
But Abraham envisioned it, as Ruben just said.

63
01:19:07.434 --> 01:19:13.434
Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, then we have Moses who frees everyone and we are going to the promised land.

64
01:19:13.434 --> 01:19:16.434
Then we are finally in the promised land.

65
01:19:16.434 --> 01:19:21.434
By the way, Moses also gives, and this is important, Moses gives the law.

66
01:19:21.434 --> 01:19:29.434
When we talk about Moses in open church, when we read about Moses in the Bible, you always have to think carefully about yourself.

67
